3.3. Multi-View ReID Feature Extraction
Appearance features are crucial for tracking tasks, especially for cross-view tracking, since object appearances from different cameras might differ due to varied illuminations and viewing angles. The na ̈ıve way to obtain the appearance feature for each 3D detection from BEVFormer is to project the 3D bounding box to each camera image and extract ReID features by the projected box. However, the projected 3D bounding boxes are usually much larger than the actual objects in the image (see Fig. 3). This will include noisy background or other nearby objects in the target object so that affect the quality of the ReID features. Therefore, we propose a 2D-3D detection association algorithm to effectively find the best 2D bounding box for each 3D detection.
